gine/godot/issues/comments/3785853844","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115273#issuecomment-3785853844","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115273","id":3785853844,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hp4uU","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T17:55:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T18:00:53Z","body":"Note that is only required when not using static typing, but that is a relevant case, the change should probably be to print what type it is, as it's impossible to detect what invalid type might have been passed as that happens outside of the call (naturally this is handled properly with a compile time error in C++, assuming you don't just pass a `Variant`)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785853844/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785912335","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115273#issuecomment-3785912335","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115273","id":3785912335,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hqHAP","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T18:04:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T18:04:41Z","body":"> Note that is only required when not using static typing, but that is a relevant case, the change should probably be to print what type it is, as it's impossible to detect what invalid type might have been passed as that happens outside of the call\r\n\r\nIf we wanted to detect this at runtime and have a generic message for any incorrect type passed to any function, I think it would need to happen in `VariantCaster<T>::cast()` (which I guess we would need to specialize for `RequiredPtr<T>` afterall)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3785912335/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket"